{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099890-sub-sphere-of-prime-optimized-for-conjunctional-effects","id":1099890,"title":"Sub-Sphere of Prime optimized for conjunctional effects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-03T12:49:11-07:00","id":1099890,"title":"Sub-Sphere of Prime optimized for conjunctional effects","content":"<span style=\"color:#F3F3F3\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">know that Primal</span></span><br /> I know that Primal Utility is like the Prime Sphere, except it's optimized for getting Quintessence out of united groups of people, rather than mystic places. I'm curious what it would look like if a sub-Sphere of Prime was optimized primarily for use with other Spheres in Effects? What could it do that standard Prime couldn't, and where would it be deficient? Also: what type of paradigm is likely to use this sub-Sphere? <br /> <span style=\"color:#F3F3F3\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Utility is like the Prime Sphere, except it's optimized for getting Quintessence out of united groups of people, rather than mystic places. I'm curious what it would look like if a sub-Sphere of Prime was optimized primarily for use with other Spheres in Effects? What could it do that standard Prime couldn't, and where would it be deficient? Also: what type of paradigm is likely to use this sub-Sphere? </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2176,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","user":"SpectacularTentacular","date":". 06-03-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T10:19:44-07:00","id":1100167,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean by this. Could you give an example? <br /> <br /> Or, potentially, as a way to frame the discussion, is Primal Utility an example of what you're talking about? As it is, effectively, Prime sensu strico retasked to obtain energies from an alternative source (human endeavor as opposed to &quot;plugging into the grid&quot; as it were). Perhaps that is a sort of Prime &quot;sub-Sphere&quot; that has been optimized for use with Entropy/Mind situations (I'm thinking of those as exemplifyhing organized, coordinated, thought shaped activity.... I guess it could be just Entropy, but that takes out the intrinsic human element. Or it could be Life, but that would seem to imply an explicit vitality-draining component that doesn't <i>have </i>to be involved, though it sure can be and often is...)<br /> <br /> Or do you mean something else completely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T10:26:40-07:00","id":1100170,"title":"","content":"I think op just wants to make a sub sphere to cover the need to have prime to fuel other effects without having the full blown prime sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T10:27:55-07:00","id":1100171,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, you can entirely ditch Prime and just add the relevant bits to the other Spheres. And get rid of Entropy while you're at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T10:39:38-07:00","id":1100173,"title":"","content":"A Technocrat Inspired Philosophy (or something) Prime variant which focuses on empowering an NWO's members Time, Entropy, Mind, and Correspondence (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/986539-the-masses-as-an-amplifier\">of directing Agents</a>). It would also have Procedures blurring Prime, Life, Mind for enhancing the body and the mind of the user. And also usable to make better Mind/Entropy texts. I dunno what it could do at Prime 5 - create a Node maybe, somehow?<br /> <br /> Another Technocratic variant for mass production out of Prime Energy and for powering Devices and Procedures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T11:54:41-07:00","id":1100187,"title":"","content":"You want a Sub-Sphere of Prime optimized primarily for use with other Spheres in Effects...<br /> <br /> That's what Prime is. Prime it'the most conjunctionable Sphere there is, you need to call it to summon stuff and energy, to infuse patterns with magic to do most types of countermagic, and to do stuff that the ST regards as &quot;manipulation of magical forces&quot;. Every Sphere beneffits, more or less, from Prime, and viceversa. And everything beneffits from Quntessence. In contrast, Prime alone and devoid of surrounding magic to affect can do very few things, usually in a quite vulgar fashion.<br /> <br /> Prime it's already optimized to work with other spheres, what would you want to change?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T17:53:18-07:00","id":1102160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099890-sub-sphere-of-prime-optimized-for-conjunctional-effects?p=1100187#post1100187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want a Sub-Sphere of Prime optimized primarily for use with other Spheres in Effects...<br /> <br /> That's what Prime is. Prime it'the most conjunctionable Sphere there is, you need to call it to summon stuff and energy, to infuse patterns with magic to do most types of countermagic, and to do stuff that the ST regards as &quot;manipulation of magical forces&quot;. Every Sphere beneffits, more or less, from Prime, and viceversa. And everything beneffits from Quntessence. In contrast, Prime alone and devoid of surrounding magic to affect can do very few things, usually in a quite vulgar fashion.<br /> <br /> Prime it's already optimized to work with other spheres, what would you want to change?.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just thinking of what it could do better than straight Prime without being game-breaking, and what it would not be so good at. This is primarily a thought exercise on my part. Nonetheless, if you (the reader) were attempting this, I'm curious to know what special thing you'd add and what you'd penalize. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T19:08:19-07:00","id":1102170,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that the extant alternate Spheres are based on in-universe concepts that are a basis for modifying the core Sphere. The differences between Prime and Primal Utility are something a Syndicate member could theoretically explain.<br /> <br /> What you're asking doesn't have that. It's a &quot;sub-Sphere&quot; based solely on mechanical game concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T07:52:28-07:00","id":1102265,"title":"","content":"I'm with Heavy. The Spheres already occupy a very weird hybrid place or double existence in Mage, as both in-game concepts and as part of the above-the-table rules. Meaning, a Sphere doesn't just exist as an artifact of the rules (like Dexterity), if you have a Sphere/specialty Sphere/alternate Sphere/sub-Sphere it's existence is known to the characters, player and non-, in the context of the game world. <br /> <br /> That's why Primal Utility functions. It's as per Dataweaver and Heavy's statements: (Data) It functionally behaves differently in a quasi-balanced way by swapping in and out certain aspects of the core Sphere and altering and/or deleting others. (Heavy) It's a different &quot;take&quot; on the same concepts that makes total sense to the ur-Focus/old style Sect level paradigms in-game; in that a Syndicate member could sit down and talk (perhaps with an It-X to keep those ur-Foci close) about how Primal Utility and Prime are different <br /> <br /> A different take on Prime might be something like a Celestial Chorister version that sees Quintessence and Patterns in terms of the presence of the divine. The current Prime is VERY Hermetic, replete with all sorts of Platonic thought that, while it has been used in religion from time to time, doesn't really segue with a lot of concepts of divine power/presence/plan. So, something like Divine Essence or Essence, that would be something like Prime (all that movement and investment of power and the creations of patterns) and something like Primal Utility (in that it makes sense to take out business-style endeavors and swap it for an ability to similarly derive Quintessence from acts of worship, a la a congregation or otherwise) and might lose out on some aspects of personally commanding such forces and more of a surrender to things happen (say, less ability to make magic items or the like).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}